## Summary

Implemented **`DET.CHROME.BOUNDARY`** as a deterministic chrome-vs-main separation check, registered it in the blender, and added unit tests. Shell commands could not be run in this environment (`Rejected`), so please run verification locally.

### Rule signal (from docs)

Chrome regions (header, footer, sidebars) must be **visually separated** from the main content canvas using at least one of: **border**, **distinct background**, or **box-shadow** (including `::before` / `::after` separators).

### Implementation (`det-chrome-boundary.check.js`)

- **`collectChromeBoundaryReport(page)`** — In the browser, finds visible chrome roots outside `main` (`header`, `footer`, `.forge-sidebar`, `.site-header`, `.landing-header`, `[data-shell-region]`, etc.), skips modals/cookies, and only checks regions that overlap the main column.
- **Pass cues** (any one counts):
  - Visible border on any edge
  - Non-trivial `box-shadow`
  - Background luminance delta ≥ `0.06` vs main canvas
  - Pseudo-element border/shadow/fill
- **`findingsFromChromeBoundaryReport`** — Maps violations to standard findings (`severity: warn`, `area: informationArchitecture`, evidence + remediation).
- **`run({ metrics, page, url })`** — Uses `metrics.chromeBoundaryReport` or live collection via Playwright (same pattern as card-title / ambient-z-index).

Exported helpers (`parseRgb`, `borderEdgeVisible`, `chromeBoundaryCuesFromStyles`, …) support unit tests without a browser.

### Registration (`rule-mappings.js`)

| Field | Value |
|--------|--------|
| `status` | `implemented` |
| `area` | `informationArchitecture` |
| `scoreDimension` | `visualRhythmFirstScreen` |
| `defaultSeverity` | `warn` |
| `priorityWeight` | `7` |

`registry.generated.json` already lists this rule as **implemented** (likely from a prior blend).

### Tests (`auditor-tests/det-chrome-boundary.test.js`)

Covers cue detection, finding shape, and `run()` with injected metrics.

